.Dd September 27, 2026
.Dt SSHD.CONF 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm sshd.conf
.Nd SSH server policy file
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Pa /etc/rach2/sshd.conf
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Init reads
.Pa /etc/rach2/sshd.conf
before starting the SSH server, which is Dropbear, or OpenSSH's
.Xr sshd 8
on the GNU system's root.
Root password logins are disabled by default.
The file has one setting:
.Dl root-password-login yes
This setting makes init start Dropbear without
.Fl g ,
and
.Xr sshd 8
with
.Ql PermitRootLogin yes
in place of
.Ql PermitRootLogin prohibit-password ,
permitting root to log in with a password.
The line
.Ql root-password-login yesterday
does not enable password login.
Only trailing whitespace may follow
.Ql root-password-login yes ;
additional text disables that line.
If the file is absent, root may log in by key only.
.Pp
The RAM images and recovery contain no such file.
.Xr rach2-install 8
writes it on the installed root, and
.Fl Fl update
preserves it when replacing the root file system.
.Pp
Dropbear generates a missing host key at the first connection, and init
runs
.Ql ssh-keygen -A
before each start of
.Xr sshd 8 ,
which makes the keys missing from
.Pa /etc/ssh .
A RAM root therefore has new keys each boot, and an installed root keeps
its own.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /home/NAME/.ssh/authorized_keys
.It Pa /etc/rach2/sshd.conf
SSH login policy read by init.
.It Pa /root/.ssh/authorized_keys
Keys authorized to log in as root.
.It Pa /home/NAME/.ssh/authorized_keys
Keys authorized to log in as the account
.Ar NAME .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr recovery 7 ,
.Xr dropbear 8 ,
.Xr init 8 ,
.Xr rach2-install 8 ,
.Xr sshd 8
